  "story": {
    "headline": "Refund and dispute webhooks now claim their event id before touching the ledger.",
    "paragraph": "Stripe redelivers a webhook until it receives a 2xx, and a slow first attempt can succeed after the retry has already been sent. On 2 August that produced a second `record_refund` call for 14 orders. This change introduces `EventClaim`, which inserts the Stripe event id into `webhook_events` with `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`; the insert either wins and returns True, or loses and returns False. `handle_refund` claims before it writes to the ledger, so a second delivery returns 200 without side effects. The same guard was added to `handle_dispute`, which the description does not mention.",
    "confidence": "high",
    "evidence": [
      "pr_description",
      "linked_issue",
      "commit_messages",
      "code"
    ],
